# The root .gitignore now anchors its pattern as `/data/`, so src/data/ -- where
# the export loaders live -- is no longer swallowed. This re-inclusion is kept as
# a guard: an unanchored `data/` there matches that name at ANY depth, and the
# failure is silent, since the whole data layer still builds and runs while being
# absent from the commit. Re-including the directory has to come before anything
# inside it can be re-included.
!/src/data/
